# ---- RV-IM100: RTL, Vivado projects, verification harness and measured data ----
# The repository is self-contained: every number in the workbooks can be
# regenerated from here alone.  What is ignored below is regenerable output.

# Vivado build output under the projects: regenerable from the sources, and the
# routed .dcp checkpoints in particular are what silently drove incremental
# implementation and broke reproducibility.  The .gen output products are
# regenerated from the .xci files in <project>.srcs.
RV-IM100_RTL/**/*.runs/
RV-IM100_RTL/**/*.cache/
RV-IM100_RTL/**/*.sim/
RV-IM100_RTL/**/*.hw/
RV-IM100_RTL/**/*.ip_user_files/
RV-IM100_RTL/**/*.gen/
# Vivado per-session scratch directories.  The path embeds the PID and the
# machine hostname.
**/.Xil/

# Working copies made by the frequency sweep: each is a throwaway clone of a
# project, implemented at a candidate clock so the measured project is never
# disturbed.
RV-IM100_RTL/project_files/.sweep/
# Throwaway project copies used to test memory-configuration changes in
# isolation.
RV-IM100_RTL/project_files/.memtest/
# Per-benchmark Embench project copies: regenerable from the variant's
# CoreMark project plus build_embench_fpga.sh and the harness.
RV-IM100_RTL/**/*_Embench_*/

# Vivado design checkpoints.  Excluded for a specific reason, not only size:
# a routed .dcp sitting under <project>.srcs/utils_1/imports/impl_1/ is picked
# up by Vivado as an AutoIncremental reference, so implementation starts from a
# previous routed design instead of from the sources.  That made repeated runs
# of the same configuration disagree, and it is invisible unless you read the
# run log.  Checkpoints are regenerable from the sources; keeping them out means
# a clone cannot inherit the problem.
*.dcp
# Vivado binary report archives: same content as the .rpt text reports beside
# them, which stay tracked and are readable and diffable.
*.rpx
*.pb

# Regenerable simulation artifacts
riscof-env/build/
riscof-env/work/
riscof-env/riscof_work/
# (riscof-env/sim/ holds tb_sim_top.cpp -- source, tracked)
# Verilator builds of the comparison-core throughput simulators.
comparison_cores/throughput/build/sim_*/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# Editor / OS
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.~lock.*#

# Large binaries that should never enter history
*.bit
*.vcd
*.elf
*.o
*.disass
*.py.bak
node_modules/
# SAIF simulation artifacts: netlists, SDF, xsim snapshots and captured SAIF are
# large and regenerable. The results/ summaries and the scripts are what matter.
riscof-env/saif/*/netlist.v
riscof-env/saif/*/netlist.sdf
riscof-env/saif/*/xsim.dir/
# kernel.saif is the MEASURED switching activity behind every power number.
# Regenerating one takes ~30 min and is not bit-identical across tool versions,
# so the captures are archived rather than treated as regenerable.
# kernel.saif IS tracked; the windowed intermediates are not.
riscof-env/saif/*/win_*.saif
riscof-env/saif/*/w[0-9].saif
riscof-env/saif/*/activity.saif
riscof-env/saif/*/live.saif
riscof-env/saif/*/*.wdb
riscof-env/saif/*/glbl.v
riscof-env/saif/rtl_probe/
riscof-env/saif/*/*.log
riscof-env/saif/*/*.tcl
riscof-env/saif/*/*.v

# Comparison cores: upstream sources are fetched, not vendored.  What matters
# for reproducibility is the exact commit/version, the synthesis wrapper, the
# constraint and the generator script -- all of which ARE tracked.  The upstream
# trees, the sbt build output and the downloaded archive are not.
comparison_cores/picorv32/
comparison_cores/rvcorep/
comparison_cores/rvcorep_orig/
comparison_cores/rvcorep_orig.zip
comparison_cores/VexRiscv/
# SAIF re-captures (saif_v2): same policy as saif/ above. kernel.saif and the
# power reports are the measurement and stay tracked; netlists, SDF, waveform
# databases and xsim snapshots are large and regenerable.
riscof-env/saif_v2/**/netlist.v
riscof-env/saif_v2/**/netlist.sdf
riscof-env/saif_v2/**/*.wdb
riscof-env/saif_v2/**/xsim.dir/
# Verilator builds of the T6 trigger-monitor and T8 stall-accounting
# simulators: regenerable from riscof-env/scripts.
riscof-env/build_t6/
riscof-env/build_t8/
